notes.body:
I originally structured the guids_delete_guid similar to the guids_add_guid. But after digging in, it seems like wmem_tree_array is simply using key\[3\] (for GUID) as its insertkey.

Although - I worry that deviating from that contract could come back to bite if the wmem_tree_insert32_array internals ever change.

I've tested the code below and it works. Should I proceed with that or stick to the previous?

```plaintext
void
guids_delete_guid(const e_guid_t *guid)
{
	guint32 g;

	/* Previous wmem_tree_insert32_array results in g[3] being used as the insert key */
	g = guid->data4[4];
	g <<= 8;
	g |= guid->data4[5];
	g <<= 8;
	g |= guid->data4[6];
	g <<= 8;
	g |= guid->data4[7];

	wmem_tree_remove32(guid_to_name_tree, g);
}
```

